WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.000


2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
<b>Arjuna sees killing his kinsmen as a grave sin.</b>

3
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.750
<b>Here, he says that instead of fighting</b>
<b>such a war against Dhritarashtra's sons,</b>

4
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:45.833
<b>it would be better if he were slain by them,</b>
<b>unarmed and without resistance.</b>

5
00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:50.541


6
00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:52.166
<b>Imagine this as a</b>

7
00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:57.458
<b>two-way conversation happening</b>
<b>in Arjuna's mind,</b>

8
00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:03.541
<b>where he's responding to Krishna's questions</b>
<b>and countering His arguments.</b>

9
00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:05.583
<b>It's as if Krishna is saying,</b>

10
00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:09.166
<b>"Arjuna, your heart resists this war,</b>

11
00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:11.375
<b>but the Kauravas are ready</b>

12
00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:12.958
<b>What will you do in this situation?"</b>

13
00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:14.583
<b>And Arjuna replies,</b>

14
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:15.750
<b>"Madhava,</b>

15
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.958
<b>the Kauravas are also my kin,</b>

16
00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:20.833
<b>and the mere thought of killing them</b>

17
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:22.916
<b>has already stained me with sin."</b>

18
00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:30.208
<b>Now, the only way to atone for this sin seems</b>
<b>to be not raising arms against them in battle,</b>

19
00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.041
<b>not to struggle.</b>

20
00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:34.166
<b>Let them do as they wish.</b>

21
00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:35.166
<b>"But Arjuna,</b>

22
00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:38.250
<b>how will this benefit you?"</b>

23
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.250
<b>"Madhava, </b>

24
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.708
<b>at the very least, I can depart</b>
<b>this life with a peaceful mind, </b>

25
00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:47.791
<b>knowing that while still alive,</b>
<b>I atoned for my sin..."</b>

26
00:01:47.791 --> 00:01:49.291
<b>What anguish this is,</b>

27
00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:53.375
<b>what a dilemma,</b>
<b>and how great is Arjuna's distress... </b>

28
00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:59.666
<b>He has convinced himself that not fighting,</b>
<b>willingly giving up his life, is the right path... </b>

29
00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:00.333
<b>But</b>

30
00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:03.708
<b>this thought is completely</b>
<b>odds with truth and righteousness... </b>

31
00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:04.291
<b>Yes,</b>

32
00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:06.333
<b>entirely at odds.</b>

33
00:02:06.916 --> 00:02:13.791


34
00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:16.250
<b>he's ready to give up.</b>

35
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.250
<b>The desire to fight has left his heart.</b>

36
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.708
<b>He's the world's greatest archer,</b>

37
00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:30.416
<b>but if his mind refuses to use that skill,</b>

38
00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:36.083
<b>how can he lift his bow and loose his arrows?</b>

39
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:41.791
<b>One may be brimming with</b>
<b>skill, ability and talent.</b>

40
00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:46.875
<b>The body may know well how to use them.</b>

41
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:54.375
<b>But if the mind that directs</b>
<b>this body itself is defeated? </b>

42
00:02:54.375 --> 00:02:56.916
<b>what remains then?</b>

43
00:02:56.916 --> 00:03:00.500
<b>This often happens in life.</b>

44
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.291
<b>It may have happened to you,</b>

45
00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:05.916
<b>or it may happen in the future,</b>

46
00:03:05.916 --> 00:03:08.916
<b>where the mind feels weak,</b>

47
00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:13.625
<b>and there's no desire to</b>
<b>use any of your abilities...</b>

48
00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:16.500
<b>Remembering Arjuna's state,</b>

49
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.833
<b>ask yourself two questions:</b>

50
00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.291
<b>First question</b>

51
00:03:23.291 --> 00:03:26.750
<b>Is Arjuna lacking in talent?</b>

52
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.500
<b>No, right? </b>

53
00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.125
<b>Neither are you.</b>

54
00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:32.083
<b>There's no lack of talent.</b>

55
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:34.000
<b>Second question</b>

56
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.083
<b>There's no shortage of talent, </b>

57
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:37.750
<b> but sometimes,</b>

58
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.166
<b>like Arjuna,</b>

59
00:03:39.166 --> 00:03:44.875
<b>isn't it better to not participate</b>

60
00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:47.833
<b>If the mind is unwilling,</b>

61
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:52.583
<b>is it still necessary to struggle?</b>

62
00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:58.166
<b>The answer will come when you</b>
<b>step back from yourself</b>

63
00:03:58.166 --> 00:03:59.458
<b>and think</b>

64
00:03:59.458 --> 00:04:02.375
<b>about what's right for the future,</b>

65
00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.375
<b>what's right for dharma.</b>

66
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:10.625
<b>Will abandoning the struggle now</b>
<b>truly bring happiness in the future?</b>

67
00:04:10.625 --> 00:04:11.666
<b>Or</b>

68
00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:19.166
<b>is giving up the struggle merely to</b>
<b>calm the anxiety of this moment?</b>

69
00:04:19.166 --> 00:04:24.416
<b>If a struggle is necessary for the future,</b>
<b>for dharma,</b>

70
00:04:24.416 --> 00:04:27.125
<b>then engage in that struggle.</b>

71
00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:29.666
<b>The talent within you is boundless...</b>

72
00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:34.291


73
00:04:34.291 --> 00:04:37.291
<b>For a moral person like Arjuna,</b>

74
00:04:37.291 --> 00:04:39.791
<b>is it right to not oppose unrighteousness,</b>

75
00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:47.166
<b>and instead surrender to unrighteous forces, </b>

76
00:04:47.166 --> 00:04:50.416
<b>is this correct?</b>

77
00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:54.333
<b>Is this truly non-violence,</b>

78
00:04:54.333 --> 00:04:57.666
<b>as Arjuna believes?</b>

79
00:04:57.666 --> 00:05:00.791
<b>Will society benefit from this?</b>

80
00:05:00.791 --> 00:05:03.250
<b>Will it bring well-being to others?</b>

81
00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:09.541
<b>Any action that promotes unrighteousness</b>
<b>doesn't bring welfare to society.</b>

82
00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:13.791
<b>So, should violence be used?</b>

83
00:05:13.791 --> 00:05:17.000
<b>We must understand that no object, </b>

84
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.875
<b>no medium is inherently right or wrong.</b>

85
00:05:19.875 --> 00:05:26.916
<b>Right and wrong depends on the intention</b>
<b>in the mind of the one using that medium..</b>

86
00:05:26.916 --> 00:05:28.041
<b>For instance,</b>

87
00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:30.500
<b>a sharp knife </b>

88
00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.708
<b> in the hands of a murderer</b>

89
00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:35.083
<b>can take a life, </b>

90
00:05:35.083 --> 00:05:36.208
<b>but</b>

91
00:05:36.208 --> 00:05:37.625
<b>the same knife</b>

92
00:05:37.625 --> 00:05:48.916
<b>when used by a surgeon</b>
<b>to cut someone's skin for treatment </b>

93
00:05:48.916 --> 00:05:50.666
<b>The knife is the same.</b>

94
00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:52.541
<b>The medium is the same.</b>

95
00:05:52.541 --> 00:05:54.291
<b>It's the different intentions</b>

96
00:05:54.291 --> 00:05:58.791
<b>that make the action right or wrong.</b>

97
00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:03.416
<b>And in social situations,</b>
<b>this is the correct method of evaluation </b>

98
00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:06.250
<b>how pure is your intention.</b>

99
00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.125
<b>If you see unrighteousness occurring, </b>

100
00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:10.708
<b>if you see someone being oppressed,</b>

101
00:06:10.708 --> 00:06:14.541
<b>it's right to raise your voice against it.</b>

102
00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:20.791
<b>If someone needs to be punished</b>
<b>through legal procedures, </b>

103
00:06:20.791 --> 00:06:22.666
<b>that is right.</b>

104
00:06:23.291 --> 00:06:27.458


105
00:06:27.458 --> 00:06:31.958
<b>In our professional lives, we often find</b>
<b>find ourselves caught in this dilemma.</b>

106
00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:38.250
<b>Should we always remain quiet,</b>
<b>ignoring disagreements? </b>

107
00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.000
<b>But </b>

108
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.625
<b>if we keep doing this,</b>

109
00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:44.166
<b>there's a fear that people</b>
<b>will forget our importance.</b>

110
00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:47.541
<b>Even our valid points will go unheard.</b>

111
00:06:47.541 --> 00:06:48.916
<b>So then,</b>

112
00:06:48.916 --> 00:06:52.500
<b>should we fight over</b>
<b>every small disagreement? </b>

113
00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.791
<b>But in this case,</b>

114
00:06:53.791 --> 00:06:56.250
<b>people will start fearing you,</b>

115
00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.625
<b>avoiding you.</b>

116
00:06:58.625 --> 00:07:04.250
<b>To resolve this dilemma,</b>
<b>we must pass through two doors.</b>

117
00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.708
<b>Does your idea,</b>

118
00:07:05.708 --> 00:07:07.166
<b>your suggestion</b>

119
00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:11.750
<b>align with the organization's long-term goals? </b>

120
00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:15.958
<b>Does it help take the organization there?</b>

121
00:07:15.958 --> 00:07:17.666
<b>The second door</b>

122
00:07:17.666 --> 00:07:21.583
<b>Is this disagreement personal?</b>

123
00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:24.708
<b>If your disagreement isn't personal, </b>

124
00:07:24.708 --> 00:07:29.333
<b>if your suggestion is good for</b>
<b>the organization's objectives, </b>

125
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:34.166
<b>then present your ideas with full conviction.</b>

126
00:07:34.166 --> 00:07:37.291
<b>Occasionally, this might lead to debate,</b>

127
00:07:37.291 --> 00:07:38.541
<b>but</b>

128
00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:42.791
<b>these very doors will be useful</b>
<b>at every step of the debate...</b>

129
00:07:42.791 --> 00:07:45.583
<b>The disagreement should not become personal.</b>

130
00:07:45.583 --> 00:07:51.875
<b>And ideas coming from both sides</b>
<b>should align with the organization's objectives.</b>

131
00:07:51.875 --> 00:07:53.291
<b>If it remains so,</b>

132
00:07:53.291 --> 00:07:55.958
<b>then this debate is logical,</b>

133
00:07:55.958 --> 00:07:58.666
<b>good for the organization.</b>

